From 201f87b37dad0541e68d4e1657d84ae5af108d15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: retrorepair <joelwhybrow@googlemail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:43:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] input: GunCal's check page has TRY AGAIN and EXIT boxes; the
 calibration is saved only on EXIT

After the five shots the calibration was saved at once and the check page said "press A or B", which nobody could tell. Now the check page has two
boxes; a pull there flashes the screen white and the gun's readings in the flash (never where it pointed before the flash) are tested against the
boxes, exactly like a calibration shot. EXIT saves the calibration and loads the menu core, TRY AGAIN starts over, and nothing is saved before
EXIT. A on the gun does what EXIT does, B saves and shows the monitor page. Host tests cover the flash, the boxes and the save.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
